    <script type="application/ld+json" set:html={JSON.stringify({
      "@context": "https://schema.org",
      "@type": "FAQPage",
      "mainEntity": [
        { "@type": "Question", "name": "What is the best email marketing software in 2026?", "acceptedAnswer": { "@type": "Answer", "text": "The best email marketing software in 2026 depends on your business. Klaviyo wins for ecommerce brands that need deep Shopify/WooCommerce data, granular segmentation, and abandoned cart automations. HubSpot Marketing Hub wins for businesses that want an all-in-one CRM + marketing automation platform. Mailchimp wins for SMBs just starting out that want a free tier, a simple builder, and a clean interface. ActiveCampaign wins for B2B and complex lifecycle automations. Brevo wins for the best combination of marketing campaigns + transactional email at a low price per volume." } },
        { "@type": "Question", "name": "Is Mailchimp still the best email platform for small businesses?", "acceptedAnswer": { "@type": "Answer", "text": "Mailchimp is still one of the best email platforms for small businesses in 2026, but it now has strong competitors. Mailchimp's free tier (500 contacts / 1,000 sends per month), its drag-and-drop builder, and its all-in-one website + commerce tools make it the easiest first pick for new businesses. However, Klaviyo beats Mailchimp on ecommerce-specific segmentation and predictive analytics, Brevo beats Mailchimp on per-email pricing at higher volume, and HubSpot beats Mailchimp on CRM integration and lifecycle marketing automation. Read our Mailchimp vs Klaviyo comparison for the full ecommerce trade-off." } },
        { "@type": "Question", "name": "Which email marketing platform has the best deliverability in 2026?", "acceptedAnswer": { "@type": "Answer", "text": "Deliverability depends more on sender reputation, list hygiene, and authentication (SPF, DKIM, DMARC) than on the platform itself. Among major platforms in 2026, Klaviyo, Postmark/Transactional, Brevo, and ActiveCampaign consistently score well on deliverability benchmarks because they enforce strict anti-spam policies and offer built-in warm-up and list-cleaning features. Mailchimp has historically had higher spam folder rates on shared IPs at low sending volumes, but its Premium tier with dedicated IPs matches peers. Always start with a small sending volume and warm up a new sender domain over 4–6 weeks regardless of the platform." } },
        { "@type": "Question", "name": "How much should I budget for email marketing software?", "acceptedAnswer": { "@type": "Answer", "text": "For up to 1,000 contacts you can run email marketing for $0–$30/month using the free tiers of Mailchimp, Brevo, HubSpot Marketing Free, or Klaviyo Free. For 1,000–10,000 contacts, budget $25–$150/month depending on features: Klaviyo (~$45/mo for 5k contacts) or HubSpot Starter ($45/mo) are the most common choices. For 10,000–100,000 contacts, budget $150–$800/month — ActiveCampaign, Klaviyo, and HubSpot Professional all sit in this range. At 100k+ contacts, pricing becomes negotiable and you should evaluate enterprise quotes plus transactional email costs separately." } }
      ]
    })} />
