      <h2 id="buying-guide">Buying Guide: Pick the Right Email Platform in 10 Minutes</h2>
      <p>Start with your primary use case and then validate against your contact tier and existing stack:</p>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Ecommerce / DTC brands (any size):</strong> Start with Klaviyo. If you are pre-launch or under $500k/yr GMV, Klaviyo Free → Klaviyo $30 tier gives you the same flows that 8-figure brands run. Fall back to Mailchimp only if you value simplicity over deep segmentation.</li>
        <li><strong>SMBs / solopreneurs launching a newsletter + store:</strong> Start with Mailchimp Free. The website, domain, and commerce tools bundled in the free tier let a new business ship a brand identity and a newsletter in one weekend. Migrate when you hit 10k+ contacts and the price per contact crosses Klaviyo or Brevo.</li>
        <li><strong>B2B SaaS / Lifecycle / RevOps teams:</strong> Start with HubSpot Marketing Starter if you are already on HubSpot CRM; otherwise start with ActiveCampaign Lite for the deepest automation library without enterprise pricing.</li>
        <li><strong>High-volume senders or transactional-heavy apps:</strong> Start with Brevo. The unlimited-contacts pricing model and the shared transactional + marketing infrastructure are unique in 2026 and cannot be matched by Mailchimp or Klaviyo.</li>
        <li><strong>Marketing + sales + service unified on one platform:</strong> Start with HubSpot Marketing Hub Starter, then evaluate Professional at 50+ employees. The cross-hub attribution pays for itself once marketing and sales share goals.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>Common mistakes to avoid: do not buy an enterprise tier on day one — every platform has a migration path, and overbuying is the #1 waste in email marketing spend; do not pick Mailchimp for a 500k-contact ecommerce store without benchmarking Klaviyo's flows and CLV reporting; and do not ignore sender authentication — SPF/DKIM/DMARC setup and a 4–6 week warm-up matter more than the platform for actual inbox placement.</p>
      <p>Learn more about our <a href="/how-we-test/">testing methodology</a> and <a href="/editorial-policy/">editorial policy</a>.</p>

      <h2 id="faq">Frequently Asked Questions</h2>
      <div class="faq">
        <details>
          <summary>What is the best email marketing software in 2026?</summary>
          <p>The best email marketing software in 2026 depends on your business. Klaviyo wins for ecommerce brands that need deep Shopify/WooCommerce data, granular segmentation, and abandoned cart automations. HubSpot Marketing Hub wins for businesses that want an all-in-one CRM + marketing automation platform. Mailchimp wins for SMBs just starting out that want a free tier, a simple builder, and a clean interface. ActiveCampaign wins for B2B and complex lifecycle automations. Brevo wins for the best combination of marketing campaigns + transactional email at a low price per volume.</p>
        </details>
        <details>
          <summary>Is Mailchimp still the best email platform for small businesses?</summary>
          <p>Mailchimp is still one of the best email platforms for small businesses in 2026, but it now has strong competitors. Mailchimp's free tier (500 contacts / 1,000 sends per month), its drag-and-drop builder, and its all-in-one website + commerce tools make it the easiest first pick for new businesses. However, Klaviyo beats Mailchimp on ecommerce-specific segmentation and predictive analytics, Brevo beats Mailchimp on per-email pricing at higher volume, and HubSpot beats Mailchimp on CRM integration and lifecycle marketing automation. Read our Mailchimp vs Klaviyo comparison for the full ecommerce trade-off.</p>
        </details>
        <details>
          <summary>Which email marketing platform has the best deliverability in 2026?</summary>
          <p>Deliverability depends more on sender reputation, list hygiene, and authentication (SPF, DKIM, DMARC) than on the platform itself. Among major platforms in 2026, Klaviyo, Postmark/Transactional, Brevo, and ActiveCampaign consistently score well on deliverability benchmarks because they enforce strict anti-spam policies and offer built-in warm-up and list-cleaning features. Mailchimp has historically had higher spam folder rates on shared IPs at low sending volumes, but its Premium tier with dedicated IPs matches peers. Always start with a small sending volume and warm up a new sender domain over 4–6 weeks regardless of the platform.</p>
        </details>
        <details>
          <summary>How much should I budget for email marketing software?</summary>
          <p>For up to 1,000 contacts you can run email marketing for $0–$30/month using the free tiers of Mailchimp, Brevo, HubSpot Marketing Free, or Klaviyo Free. For 1,000–10,000 contacts, budget $25–$150/month depending on features: Klaviyo (~$45/mo for 5k contacts) or HubSpot Starter ($45/mo) are the most common choices. For 10,000–100,000 contacts, budget $150–$800/month — ActiveCampaign, Klaviyo, and HubSpot Professional all sit in this range. At 100k+ contacts, pricing becomes negotiable and you should evaluate enterprise quotes plus transactional email costs separately.</p>
